🔄 Typical workflow
1. A user creates an account and completes the required verification.
2. The user logs in and receives a protected session.
3. The backend identifies the user's role and permissions.
4. The dashboard displays only the features allowed for that role.
5. The user can use permitted operational agents or the AI Copilot.
6. Important actions and access decisions can be recorded in the activity log.
7. Administrators can manage users, roles, account status and Store Manager outlet assignments.
